🧠 MYBATIS COMPLETE NOTES (FROM YOUR 5 IMAGES)
🔷 1. ADVANCED RELATIONSHIPS
✅ Types of Relationships
🔹 One-to-One
Use: <association>
Example: User → Address
Fetch strategies:
Nested Select (lazy, may cause N+1)
Nested Result (JOIN, better performance)
🔹 One-to-Many
Use: <collection>
Example: Department → Employees
Two approaches:
Nested Select → ❌ N+1 problem
Nested Result (JOIN) → ✅ Recommended
🔹 Many-to-Many
Use JOIN with mapping
Example: Student ↔ Course
Requires:
Intermediate table
<collection> inside <collection> (or flatten)
⚠️ Important Concepts
Always define <id> → avoids duplicate objects
Use column alias in JOIN
Prefer JOIN over nested select for performance
🔷 2. PARAMETER HANDLING
✅ Parameter Types
🔹 Single Parameter
User getUser(int id);
🔹 Multiple Parameters
Use @Param
User getUser(@Param("id") int id, @Param("name") String name);
🔹 POJO Parameter
Pass full object
User getUser(User user);
🔹 Map Parameter
Map<String, Object>
