🔷 3. COLLECTION MAPPING (ONE-TO-MANY)
✅ Mapping Structure
<collection property="employees" ofType="Employee">
   <id property="id" column="emp_id"/>
</collection>
🔹 Two Approaches
1. Nested Select
Executes multiple queries
❌ N+1 problem
2. Nested Result (JOIN)
Single query
✅ Best performance
⚠️ Key Notes
Always include <id> inside <collection>
MyBatis groups results automatically
Use JOIN + alias
🔷 4. INHERITANCE MAPPING (DISCRIMINATOR)
✅ Concept
Maps one table → multiple object types
Works like switch-case
🔹 Example
<discriminator column="type">
  <case value="EMP" resultType="Employee"/>
  <case value="MGR" resultType="Manager"/>
</discriminator>
⚠️ Key Points
Only ONE case executes
Column value decides object type
Useful in polymorphism
🧠 Use Case
Employee table with:
Employee
Manager
Intern
🔷 5. DYNAMIC SQL
✅ Core Tags
🔹 <if>
Conditional SQL
<if test="name != null">
  name = #{name}
</if>
🔹 <where>
Removes leading AND/OR automatically
🔹 <choose>
Works like switch-case
Only one <when> executes
🔹 <foreach>
Used for lists (IN clause, batch insert)
<foreach collection="ids" item="id" separator=",">
  #{id}
</foreach>
🔹 <set>
Used in UPDATE
Removes trailing comma
🔹 <trim>
Custom WHERE/SET behavior
⚠️ Common Mistakes
Missing <where> → broken SQL
Trailing comma in update
Wrong IN clause usage
🔷 6. PERFORMANCE & BEST PRACTICES
🚀 Best Practices
Prefer JOIN over nested select
Always define <id>
Use #{} (never ${} for values)
Use resultMap for complex queries
Use lazy loading carefully
⚠️ N+1 Problem
1 query + N extra queries
Happens in nested select
Fix: Use JOIN
🔹 Caching
First-level → SqlSession
Second-level → Mapper
